{
    "background_story": "Zaniyah was a free-spirited artist who lived life on her own terms. She rejected the conventional norms and expectations of society, embracing instead the philosophy of existentialism. For Zaniyah, life had no inherent meaning, and it was up to each individual to create their own purpose. She spent her days exploring the city, observing the human condition, and capturing its essence through her art. Her paintings were a reflection of her own search for meaning, often featuring bold, abstract strokes and vibrant colors. Zaniyah's friends and family would often describe her as enigmatic and introspective, lost in thought as she navigated the complexities of existence. Yet, in her own words, 'the absurdity of life is what makes it beautiful.' Zaniyah's art became a testament to her existentialist worldview, inspiring others to question and create their own meaning in life.",
